\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5.8}{\ignorespaces  Parity contrast versus sequence length; (a) shows the standard $Z$ measured correlated populations. (b) shows parity contrast --- a signal proportional to occupation of the symmetric-trace sector. Solid lines are multi-exponential decays given by equation~\ref {eqn:app_pops} and equation~\ref {eqn:parity_contrast} for (a) and (b) respectively. Dashed lines indicate the expected asymptotes. (c) and (d) show example parity fringes for sequences of $m=25$ and $m=1600$ Clifford gates respectively with solid lines given by equation~\ref {eqn:app_parcontrast}. }}{104}{figure.caption.51}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:k-copy_par_data}{{5.8}{104}{Parity contrast versus sequence length; (a) shows the standard $Z$ measured correlated populations. (b) shows parity contrast --- a signal proportional to occupation of the symmetric-trace sector. Solid lines are multi-exponential decays given by equation~\ref {eqn:app_pops} and equation~\ref {eqn:parity_contrast} for (a) and (b) respectively. Dashed lines indicate the expected asymptotes. (c) and (d) show example parity fringes for sequences of $m=25$ and $m=1600$ Clifford gates respectively with solid lines given by equation~\ref {eqn:app_parcontrast}}{figure.caption.51}{}}
